Hi Michel,
well, to build without the whoami-functionality, you may:
	•	Modify find_interpreter in main.c to simply return my_strdup("")
	•	Edit Makefile.am and remove whoami.c and whoami.h from yabasic_SOURCES
	•	use automake, configure, etc. as outlined in the comments
even then, yabasic may come in trouble on startup when trying to check its interpreter, so keep fingers crossed. And of course, the bind-feature will not work.
